eneity.", "Experiment runs externally (no GPUs/network here); pinned software stack is a provisioning-time prerequisite.", "Total runs = R x (core cells + included optional cells); cost formula absorbs unknown GPU/budget."], "uncertainties": ["Exact --zero-bubble-max-pending-backward parsing and 2x-PP stage-counting semantics unverified (empty workspace); re-verification is a hard gate.", "Whether ZB-2p, ZB-1P/H2/VPP baselines exist in the chosen Megatron build and their kernel naming for profiler classification.", "Actual GPU count, model size, and wall-clock budget are unknown; cell matrix and R are pruned via the cost formula once known.", "Run-to-run variance magnitude unknown; a 3-run pilot decides whether R=5 or R=10 suffices for a tight (<=1%) CI.", "Whether p2p comm always overlaps compute in the build affects comm's role in the bubble denominator; handled by separate comm-share reporting.", "No experiment was or will be executed from this container; all outcomes in the design are targets, not results."], "kind": "ReviewHandoffAction"}, "tool_name": "end_researcher_turn", "tool_call_id": "chatcmpl-tool-5eccca13aa134b02b0cb103d35a17c76", "tool_call": {"id": "chatcmpl-tool-5eccca13aa134b02b0cb103d35a17c76", "responses_item_id": null, "name": "end_researcher_turn", "arguments": "{"stage": "result", "answer": "# FINAL EXPERIMENT DESIGN \u2014 Does the automatic scheduling algorithm's ZB-2p output achieve a near-zero bubble rate in practice on multiple GPUs?\n\nStatus: **DESIGN-ONLY. No experiment has been or will be run in this deliverable.** Every factual claim below is tagged **[PROPOSED]** (a design default awaiting confirmation) or **[VERIFIED-FACT]** (observed in this workspace). Nothing about the target system's behavior has been empirically demonstrated.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Question and rationale\n\n**Question:** When the automatic pipeline-scheduling algorithm emits the \"ZB-2p\" schedule (activated by `--zero-bubble-max-pending-backward = 2 \u00d7 number of pipeline stages`), does the schedule's theoretical bubble-free property actually materialize as a near-zero bubble rate when the workload is profiled on a multi-GPU cluster?\n\n**Rationale:** Zero-bubble (ZB) pipeline scheduling removes the classic 1F1B idle bubble *under idealizing assumptions* \u2014 uniform/homogeneous stage compute times, enough micro-batches in flight to saturate the 2-pass overlap (2\u00d7P pending backward), overlappable p2p communication, and a steady-state window that excludes ramp-up/drain transients. In practice all of these can be violated (stage imbalance, memory-pressure stalls, comm serialization, GPU heterogeneity, run-to-run variance). This experiment measures the gap between the *scheduler-level theoretical timeline* and the *empirically profiled per-GPU timeline*, and tests whether the residual idle fraction is within a pre-registered \"near-zero\" bound of 2% of the steady-state window.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Definitions (agreed defaults unless noted)\n\n| Item | Definition | Tag |\n|---|---|---|\n| Bubble (empirical) | Per stage, wall time during the steady-state window when the stage's GPU is executing **no compute AND no communication kernels** (idle), while the pipeline is mid-iteration. | **[AGREED in review]** |\n| Steady-state window | Middle of an iteration, excluding micro-batch ramp-up (first batch entering the pipeline) and final drain (last batch exiting). Practical operationalization: run \u22653 warm-up iterations, then measure the middle N measured iterations; per-iteration window = from first stage's first stable backward to last stage's last forward minus drain, or equivalently the flat region of the GPU-busy time series. | **[PROPOSED]** |\n| Bubble rate (stage) | bubble_time / steady-state window duration. | **[AGREED]** |\n| Bubble rate (headline) | mean over stages; **max-over-stages** also reported as the scheduler-relevant bound (any stage's bubble caps throughput). | **[AGREED in review]** |\n| \"Near zero\" | Steady-state residual bubble rate \u2264 2% of the steady-state window, judged by a **one-sided upper confidence bound** on the mean bubble rate (primary test, \u00a76). | **[AGREED in review]** |\n| Stage count (for 2\u00d7P) | Pipeline-parallel degree PP = number of pipeline stages. Flag set to `--zero-bubble-max-pending-backward = 2 \u00d7 PP`. | **[AGREED in review; semantics from task hint + public Megatron docs, NOT verified on disk]** |\n\nVerified workspace facts: `/workspace` contains only `task.json`; no scheduler source, no Megatron tree, no profiler code, no GPUs (`gpu_enabled:false`), no network. **[VERIFIED-FACT]** Therefore all flag/schedule semantics are inherited from the task hint and public documentation and **must be re-verified against the real Megatron source before any external run** (hard prerequisite, \u00a78).\n\n---\n\n## 3. Dual-layer measurement methodology\n\nThe central idea: measure the schedule twice, once from its emitted event stream (what the algorithm *plans*) and once from execution (what the GPUs *do*); the gap between them is the \"in practice\" verdict.\n\n### Layer A \u2014 Scheduler-level theoretical timeline (deterministic)\n- Instrument the schedule emitter (Megatron `get_forward_backward_func` family) to log, per stage `s` and micro-batch `m`, the ordered events {FWD(s,m), BWD(s,m), P2P_send/recv(s)} for the ZB-2p iteration.\n- Reconstruct the ideal timeline under the scheduler's own assumptions (zero p2p latency, uniform stage durations, unbounded memory).\n- Output `bubble_theory(stage) = 1 - (sum of scheduled FWD+BWD durations)/makespan` in steady state. For ZB-2p this should be ~0 by construction; **Layer A validates the measurement pipeline, not the claim** (sanity baseline).\n\n### Layer B \u2014 Empirical per-GPU timeline (nsys + torch.profiler)\n- Profile on **non-timing iterations** (profiling disabled on the iterations used for wall-clock metrics) to avoid profiler perturbation. Concretely: run K timing iterations with only lightweight CUDA events, then 2\u20133 profiler iterations with `torch.profiler` (or `nsys profile`) attached, in an interleaved cadence (e.g., profile iterations 6\u20138 and 16\u201318 while timing iterations 5\u201320).\n- Classify each GPU's timeline inside the steady-state window into three disjoint label classes by kernel names: **compute** (matmul/attention/activation fwd-bwd kernels), **comm** (NCCL p2p/collectives), **idle** (no kernel executing).\n- Empirical bubble per stage = idle label time in the window / window duration. Aggregate mean and max over stages.\n- GPU-identity annotation records which physical GPU index runs each stage, so cross-run heterogeneity can be attributed.\n\nDesign default: both layers run for the same cells; Layer A costs near-zero and Layer B is the expensive part.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Configuration / cell matrix (prunable)\n\n### 4.1 Mandatory core matrix (runs in ALL budget scenarios)\nFactors: **baseline \u00d7 PP \u00d7 (M/P)**, uniform GPT-style stages throughout.\n\n| Dimension | Levels |\n|---|---|\n| Schedule | ZB-2p (flag = 2\u00d7PP) vs 1F1B default (non-ZB baseline) |\n| PP (pipeline stages) | 4, 8 |\n| M/P (micro-batches per stage) | 1, 2, 4 |\n| DP (data parallel) | fixed per cell (see \u00a77) |\n| Stage sizes | uniform (homogeneous) |\n\nCore cells = 2 (schedule) \u00d7 2 (PP) \u00d7 3 (M/P) = **12 schedule\u00d7config cells** on a fixed world size. World size = PP \u00d7 DP; recommend DP such that total GPUs is constant (16 or 32) so PP and DP trade off on a fixed budget.\n\n### 4.2 Optional extension matrix (only if budget allows)\n| Extension | Purpose |\n|---|---|\n| PP=16 | Probe deeper pipelines / finer granularity |\n| Non-uniform stage control | One config with unequal per-stage compute (uneven layer counts) to violate the homogeneity assumption and measure its bubble cost |\n| ZB-1P / ZB-H2 (V-shape) / interleaved VPP baselines | Attribute what 2-pass specifically buys over 1-pass and V-shape |\n| Idle-noise-floor control | A stage forced artificially busy (or an all-compute micro-benchmark) to measure the empirical floor of \"idle\" detection \u2192 sets what 2% is measured against |\n| Flag-adequacy control: `--zero-bubble-max-pending-backward \u2208 {P, 2P, 4P}` at fixed M=2P | Confirms 2\u00d7P is the saturating/prescribed value (task hint), and quantifies under-saturation (P) vs over-provisioning (4P) |\n\n### 4.3 Workload\n- Model: decoder-only GPT-style transformer (standard for Zero-Bubble literature) with hidden/config sized so that the ZB-2p 2\u00d7P in-flight state at M=2P fits memory with headroom (memory feasibility is a prerequisite check, \u00a78).\n- Global batch = M \u00d7 DP micro-batches, fixed token budget per iteration across cells for comparability.\n- Data: fixed, reproducible synthetic or cached dataset (external cluster must pin the same data; no network here).\n\n---\n\n## 5. Trials, ordering, and normalization\n\n- **Repeats:** 5 per cell when variance is low, 10 when variance is high (decision rule: run 3 pilot; if intra-cell std/mean > 10%, escalate to 10). **[PROPOSED]**\n- **Ordering:** cell-run order randomized (latin-square over repeat index) to decorrelate cluster drift and thermal state from schedule effects. **[PROPOSED]**\n- **Normalization (GPU-heterogeneity guard):** per run, record achieved FLOPS and clock throttling (nvidia-smi / DCGM) and per-iteration wall time; express bubble rate on the *normalized* steady-state window; if clocks differ by >\u00b15% between runs of a cell, flag and rerun in a quiet window. **[PROPOSED]**\n- **Repetition of same cell:** identical seed/init/data across repeats; only ambient variance (clocks, NUMA, NCCL ordering) remains.\n\nTotal-run formula (used in \u00a78): `N_runs = R \u00d7 [ C_core + C_opt_included ]`, where R = repeats (5\u201310), C_core = 12, C_opt = optional cells selected.\n\n---\n\n## 6. Analysis plan\n\n1. **Scheduler-vs-empirical validation (measurement sanity):** compare Layer A `bubble_theory` vs Layer B empirical bubble at each cell. If they disagree by more than measurement noise where theory predicts ~0, the measurement is suspect (kernel misclassification, window misalignment) \u2192 fix instrumentation before drawing conclusions. This validates the *method*, not the claim.\n2. **Primary test (the verdict):** for each core cell, compute the one-sided upper confidence bound (bootstrap percentile or t-based, \u03b1=0.05) on the mean empirical steady-state bubble rate. Claim \"near zero in practice\" for that cell iff the UCB \u2264 0.02 (2%). Report both mean-over-stages and max-over-stages UCBs; the verdict is graded by the max-over-stages bound as the scheduler-relevant limit.\n3. **Paired comparison vs baseline:** for each (PP, M/P) cell, pair the ZB-2p run and the 1F1B run from the same repeat index; Wilcoxon signed-rank on per-run bubble rates (and on per-run throughput) to show ZB-2p's reduction is statistically significant and not ambient noise.\n4. **Attribution decomposition of any residual bubble** (when UCB > 2%): split residual idle into (a) **transient share** (window-edge misfit), (b) **memory-stall / max-pending saturation share** (from flag-adequacy control: bubble falls as flag grows from P\u21922P, levels off at 2P\u21924P), (c) **comm-imbalance share**, (d) **stage-compute-imbalance share** (from non-uniform control). This determines *why* near-zero holds or fails.\n5. **Sensitivity curves:** bubble_rate vs M/P (per PP, per schedule); bubble_rate vs PP; bubble_rate vs max-pending flag value. These are the primary generalization evidence and also test the scheduler's design assumptions.\n6. **Reporting:** per cell: mean \u00b1 std bubble (mean- and max-over-stages), UCB, paired p-value, per-run normalized FLOPS/clock summary. Verdict matrix: PASS (UCB \u2264 2% at max-over-stages) / MARGINAL (mean \u2264 2% but max > 2%) / FAIL.\n\n---\n\n## 7. Target multi-GPU configurations (concrete core cells)\n\nFixed model/workload; world size held at 16 GPUs for the core matrix (32-GPU variants optional):\n\n| Cell ID | Schedule | PP | DP | M/P | M (per iter) | World size |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| A01\u2013A03 | 1F1B | 4 | 4 | 1 / 2 / 4 | 4 / 8 / 16 | 16 |\n| A04\u2013A06 | 1F1B | 8 | 2 | 1 / 2 / 4 | 2 / 4 / 8 | 16 |\n| A07\u2013A09 | ZB-2p (flag=8) | 4 | 4 | 1 / 2 / 4 | 4 / 8 / 16 | 16 |\n| A10\u2013A12 | ZB-2p (flag=16) | 8 | 2 | 1 / 2 / 4 | 2 / 4 / 8 | 16 |\n\nFlag-adequacy control overlays A07/A10: re-run with flag \u2208 {P, 4P} at fixed M=2P (2 extra cells per PP = 4 optional cells). Non-uniform control: 2 cells (PP=4, PP=8, M=2P, ZB-2p) with uneven stage layer counts. Optional P=16: +3 cells (M/P = 1,2,4) on 32 GPUs. ZB-1P/H2/VPP: +3 cells (PP=4, M=2P). Idle-floor: 1 control cell. Optional total = 9\u201313 cells; full matrix = 21\u201325 cells.\n\n---\n\n## 8. Feasibility & budget\n\n**Compute:** This container has CPU-only (224 vCPU), no GPU, no network \u2014 **[VERIFIED-FACT]**; the experiment must run on an external multi-GPU cluster (16\u201332 \u00d7 NVIDIA A100/H100, NVLink + InfiniBand).\n\n**Pinned software stack (provisioning-time prerequisite):** Megatron-LM build containing the zero-bubble schedules (`get_forward_backward_func`, `--zero-bubble-max-pending-backward` and ZB-2p selection) \u2014 exact commit pinned at provision time; matching Python + PyTorch (CUDA build); Nsight Systems (`nsys`) and/or `torch.profiler`; NCCL version; nvidia-smi/DCGM for clock + power capture; reproducible data split.\n\n**Cost formula (contingent on final budget):** `N_runs = R \u00d7 (C_core + \u03a3 optional_included)`; per-run cost \u2248 warmup_iters + measured_iters + profiler_iters, dominated by Layer-B profiler iterations. Example: full matrix R=5 \u2248 105 runs; core-only R=5 \u2248 60 runs; core-only R=10 \u2248 120 runs. With per-run \u2248 24 iterations \u00d7 T (T \u2248 2\u20135 s for GPT-style), full matrix \u2248 1\u20133 GPU-hours on 16 GPUs. The matrix is prunable in unit steps (drop optional cells, drop R to 5, or drop M/P=1 cells first) to fit any real budget.\n\n**Hard gates before running:**\n1. Re-verify flag semantics and 2\u00d7PP stage counting against the real Megatron source (unverifiable in this empty workspace).\n2. Memory-feasibility check at M=2P for the chosen model (bubble-free claim is vacuous if the 2-pass schedule OOMs and falls back).\n3. Confirm profiler kernel-name classification rules against the actual build's kernel naming.\n\n---\n\n## 9. Assumptions and uncertainties (carried, agreed framing)\n\n**Fixed facts (verified here):** workspace is empty (only task.json, no code/GPUs/network); design-only; no runs performed.\n\n**Assumptions (agreed in review):** \"near zero\" = steady-state bubble \u2264 2% via one-sided UCB on mean; bubble = GPU idle (no compute AND no comm) in steady state; stage count = PP; flag-adequacy sweep {P, 2P, 4P}; prunable matrix (core = {PP 4/8} \u00d7 {M/P 1/2/4} \u00d7 ZB-2p vs 1F1B, uniform stages) with \u22645\u201310 repeats, randomized order, per-run FLOPS/clock normalization; ZB-1P/H2/VPP + non-uniform + idle-floor + P=16 as optional; software stack pinned at provision time.\n\n**Uncertainties (to resolve only when the real environment exists):** exact flag/stage-count semantics and ZB-2p availability in the target Megatron build; actual GPU count and wall-clock budget (cost formula absorbs the range); run-to-run variance magnitude (3-run pilot decides R=5 vs 10); profiler kernel-name\u2192class mapping; whether p2p comm always overlaps compute in the chosen build (comm share reported separately so the bubble denominator ambiguity is exposed, not hidden).\n\n**Final statement:** no experiment has been executed; this design, if approved, defines exactly how the near-zero-bubble claim for ZB-2p would be tested on a real multi-GPU cluster, with the workspace's lack of a repository explicitly noted so no scheduler or profiler internals are treated as verifie